{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019CsvPV5PBZbW4GvkQFDJfZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-15-1020-decouple-vpmm-pool-threshold\n2\t\n3\tDecouple the VPMM allocation routing threshold from the physical page size by introducing a separate `pool_threshold` parameter. Currently, allocations smaller than `page_size` (16 MiB) use `cudaMallocAsync` while larger ones go through the VPMM page-management system. The previous page-size increase from 2 MiB to 16 MiB gave a surprising −186 ms on APC 300 STARK excl trace, with ~136 ms coming from medium-sized allocations (2–16 MiB) bypassing VPMM overhead. By raising the routing threshold to 64 MiB (4× page_size) without changing the page size itself, allocations in the 16–64 MiB range (including per-thread GKR intermediates at ~20–40 MiB each) will also bypass VPMM, avoiding per-allocation cuMemCreate, page tracking, and defragmentation overhead while preserving the 16 MiB page granularity for truly large allocations (>64 MiB).\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01CYSyLVUWASgEojr4SuTDY5","session_id":"bb5d1119-b0b0-4361-9117-64026afc483a","uuid":"86874bd7-9bc8-4798-955a-532adc446914","timestamp":"2026-04-15T08:26:57.509Z"}
